"{\n  \"diagnosis\": {\n    \"compliance_analysis\": {\n      \"evidence_refs\": [\n        \"POLICY/C002/3cd92d17ace7e93a6ae618a34c3bda7766233245904e4041a606037e246e9ff3/L11\",\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T011/R033/R1/E0010\",\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T011/R033/R1/E0011\",\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T022/R036/R1/E0011\",\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T022/R036/R1/E0012\",\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T033/R011/R1/E0010\",\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T033/R011/R1/E0011\",\n        \"PAIR/1c9245dbc681d8f84c56f7f797571dc16011aa00be2963203da114a337c5f34c/PARENT/E0005\",\n        \"PAIR/1c9245dbc681d8f84c56f7f797571dc16011aa00be2963203da114a337c5f34c/CANDIDATE/E0005\",\n        \"PAIR/1c9245dbc681d8f84c56f7f797571dc16011aa00be2963203da114a337c5f34c/CANDIDATE/E0006\"\n      ],\n      \"finding\": \"Two current single-traveler booking trajectories are task-successful but noncompliant. In both, after the user gave explicit confirmation and before the book_reservation call, the agent sent a user-visible assistant message immediately before the tool call: T011 sent 'Booking now with the confirmed details.' and then called the tool; T022 sent 'Booking now.\\\\n\\\\n' and then called the tool. The compliant current trajectory, T033, moved directly from explicit user confirmation to the book_reservation tool call with no intervening assistant message. This supports a scoped compliance relation for database-updating booking calls: after explicit confirmation, call the update tool directly rather than emitting any additional pre-tool assistant message. The historical whitespace-only contrast is narrower: parent emitted a whitespace-only pre-tool message and was noncompliant, while candidate used a substantive pre-tool message before a get_user_details read and was compliant. Therefore the current evidence is best understood as scoping the current L19-19 guidance to database-updating calls and tightening it for those calls rather than claiming every substantive pre-tool message is noncompliant.\",\n      \"supervision_refs\": [\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T011/R033/R1/S\",\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T022/R036/R1/S\",\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T033/R011/R1/S\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": [\n        \"The causal mechanism for the compliance label is not proven: it may reflect the evaluator treating a user-visible message adjacent to a tool call as a simultaneous response, rather than any property of the message text itself.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"parent_skill_gaps\": [\n      {\n        \"evidence_refs\": [\n          \"POLICY/C002/3cd92d17ace7e93a6ae618a34c3bda7766233245904e4041a606037e246e9ff3/L11\",\n          \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T011/R033/R1/E0009\",\n          \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T011/R033/R1/E0010\",\n          \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T011/R033/R1/E0011\",\n          \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T022/R036/R1/E0010\",\n          \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T022/R036/R1/E0011\",\n          \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T022/R036/R1/E0012\",\n          \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T033/R011/R1/E0010\",\n          \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T033/R011/R1/E0011\",\n          \"PAIR/1c9245dbc681d8f84c56f7f797571dc16011aa00be2963203da114a337c5f34c/PARENT/E0005\",\n          \"PAIR/1c9245dbc681d8f84c56f7f797571dc16011aa00be2963203da114a337c5f34c/CANDIDATE/E0005\",\n          \"PAIR/1c9245dbc681d8f84c56f7f797571dc16011aa00be2963203da114a337c5f34c/CANDIDATE/E0006\"\n        ],\n        \"gap\": \"Revise the current pre-tool guidance to add a condition for database-updating tool calls. When the next intended action is book_reservation, update_reservation_flights, update_reservation_baggages, update_reservation_passengers, or another booking-database update, and the user has just given explicit confirmation, do not emit another assistant message immediately before the update call; call the update tool directly. In the current group, substantive pre-tool messages such as 'Booking now with the confirmed details.' and 'Booking now.\\\\n\\\\n' occurred only in noncompliant trajectories, while the compliant trajectory called book_reservation directly after confirmation. This is a tentative empirical pattern scoped to immediate pre-update messages after confirmation; it does not require the agent to avoid substantive messages before read-only lookups or before obtaining confirmation.\",\n        \"kind\": \"NEEDS_REVISION\",\n        \"related_rule_refs\": [\n          \"RULE/0e56d1481e4ae6ba102d02fa86076216cea4fa296022a237744d8673a575e604/L19-19\"\n        ],\n        \"source_dimensions\": [\n          \"COMPLIANCE\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"skill_addressability\": {\n      \"reason\": \"Current observations provide an executable compliance gap. The existing Rule L19-19 only discourages whitespace-only pre-tool messages, but the current noncompliant cases used substantive pre-tool messages immediately before book_reservation after explicit user confirmation, while the current compliant case called the update tool directly. The concrete Agent decision is whether to insert a user-visible message between the user's confirmation and a booking-database update call, and the available trajectory contrast supports revising L19-19 to direct a call without that intervening message. This is addressable as a NEEDS_REVISION to current Parent guidance.\",\n      \"status\": \"ADDRESSABLE\"\n    },\n    \"success_analysis\": {\n      \"evidence_refs\": [\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T011/R033/R1/E0011\",\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T011/R033/R1/E0012\",\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T022/R036/R1/E0012\",\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T022/R036/R1/E0013\",\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T033/R011/R1/E0011\",\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T033/R011/R1/E0012\"\n      ],\n      \"finding\": \"All three current single-traveler booking experiences succeeded. Regardless of the differences in cabin, fare, and requested checked-bag count, each trajectory verified the user profile and available flight, quoted the fare plus the applicable $50-per-nonfree-bag charge, obtained explicit user confirmation, and called book_reservation with the saved credit card and requested bag counts. The tool results returned reservations with the expected passenger, flight, cabin, bag counts, and payment amount. No success-related deficiency is supported by the current group.\",\n      \"supervision_refs\": [\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T011/R033/R1/S\",\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T022/R036/R1/S\",\n        \"CURRENT/a5aef3b6c8a95f395a47ef382eac2d473fbc9a65b0b22d68d127bd7c93fd32f2/T033/R011/R1/S\"\n      ],\n      \"unresolved\": []\n    }\n  },\n  \"memory_review\": [\n    {\n      \"decision\": \"DEFER\",\n      \"edit_id\": \"EDIT/795a7781c8ffccc551cf5d7bb1da2baaa7791c6116db1541e573aa3bfbfbd5b2\",\n      \"evidence_refs\": [],\n      \"gap_indices\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"The passenger-count boundary guard is not implicated by the current single-traveler booking group, and no supported current Parent change requires its removal or revision. Historical review shows a mixed association, but the current evidence supplies no applicable condition for changing the existing rule beyond keeping its bounded uncertainty.\",\n      \"relation\": \"NONE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"decision\": \"DEFER\",\n      \"edit_id\": \"EDIT/b680e065ea22d503d5d4d93ae55f01c6e1938f9943a3f9f2ddabeba0787feb6f\",\n      \"evidence_refs\": [],\n      \"gap_indices\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"The settlement-channel pricing guidance concerns multi-segment itinerary modification, which is absent from the current single-traveler booking experiences. No current condition activates the rule, and no historical binding requires a current edit now.\",\n      \"relation\": \"NONE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"decision\": \"DEFER\",\n      \"edit_id\": \"EDIT/8e908eca023aed4f8ea82c6c2027470ed3e1712ab85d0fa5cebf050d3d8a9a74\",\n      \"evidence_refs\": [],\n      \"gap_indices\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"The address-propagation sequence rule belongs to retail address synchronization and does not apply to the current airline single-traveler booking group. No supported current Parent change is needed.\",\n      \"relation\": \"NONE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"decision\": \"DEFER\",\n      \"edit_id\": \"EDIT/abae1bfe258fee9184a6e6544507545829f1e5da1541e14aa028f2f13267b7f9\",\n      \"evidence_refs\": [],\n      \"gap_indices\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"The partner_direct return-over-exchange pattern concerns delivered retail orders and purchase protection, which is not present in the current airline booking group. No current binding or supported revision is warranted.\",\n      \"relation\": \"NONE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"decision\": \"USE\",\n      \"edit_id\": \"EDIT/5129358bf3bdb58719a79e072abf71e6f60a59b604b0d59d80b4b557f3888735\",\n      \"evidence_refs\": [\n        \"PAIR/1c9245dbc681d8f84c56f7f797571dc16011aa00be2963203da114a337c5f34c/PARENT/E0005\",\n        \"PAIR/1c9245dbc681d8f84c56f7f797571dc16011aa00be2963203da114a337c5f34c/CANDIDATE/E0005\",\n        \"PAIR/1c9245dbc681d8f84c56f7f797571dc16011aa00be2963203da114a337c5f34c/CANDIDATE/E0006\"\n      ],\n      \"gap_indices\": [\n        0\n      ],\n      \"reason\": \"The accepted whitespace-only pre-tool rule remains the bound current target, but current observations show it is too narrow: noncompliant current cases used substantive pre-tool messages immediately before booking updates, and the compliant current case called the update tool directly. Historical evidence shows a whitespace-only parent pre-tool message was noncompliant and candidate used a substantive message before a read-only lookup, so the useful direction is preserved while the database-update case needs scoped revision.\",\n      \"relation\": \"REVISES\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"decision\": \"DEFER\",\n      \"edit_id\": \"EDIT/a40b8e48ad121156855b690318f4a6aa38b13dfb6533167234215db402e47e62\",\n      \"evidence_refs\": [],\n      \"gap_indices\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"The certificate/gift-card payment-allocation rule is not relevant to the current group, which uses a single saved credit card for each booking. No current condition or expected edit requires changing this rule.\",\n      \"relation\": \"NONE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"decision\": \"DEFER\",\n      \"edit_id\": \"EDIT/fe8af405126b429e94f3cce8d138fb3728db8f0567e9986f97f1a0a804fc9a7c\",\n      \"evidence_refs\": [],\n      \"gap_indices\": [],\n      \"reason\": \"The post-booking-error recovery rule is not applicable to the current observations because both current bookings completed without a payment-method error. No current Parent change is supported.\",\